<title>UK: BOE gives UK money market 215 mln stg late help.</title>
<headline>BOE gives UK money market 215 mln stg late help.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of England said it provided the UK money market with around 215 million stg of unspecified late assistance.  </p>
<p>			    EARLY	1100 GMT   1300 GMT   LATE</p>
<p> FORECAST SHORTAGE    1.2 BLN    1.4 BLN    1.35 BLN   1.35 BLN</p>
<p> CUMULATIVE SUPPLY    600 MLN    650 MLN    1.11 BLN   1.325 BLN</p>
<p>DETAILS</p>
<p> BAND 1  BANK BILLS   =	    =	    459 MLN*   =</p>
<p> BAND 2  BANK BILLS   250 MLN*   =	    =	    =</p>
<p> BILLS/FRG NOV 4	350 MLN#    50 MLN#    =	   =</p>
<p> UNSPECIFIED ASSISTANCE					  215 MLN</p>
<p>* INTEREST RATE - 5-11/16 PERCENT (UNCHANGED BASE RATES)</p>
<p># INTERST RATE 5-23/32 PERCENT</p>
</text>
